# The environment variables the service honours.
#
# There is no .env loader. Nothing reads this file at runtime — it is a
# reference. install.sh writes the ones it needs into the systemd unit at
# ~/.config/systemd/user/personal-dashboard.service, and that unit's
# Environment= lines are where these actually belong. Copy what you need.
#
# Almost nothing is required. The Google client ID and secret, the Anthropic
# key and the ingest key are all entered in the Settings page instead, and
# stored encrypted in the database. The env forms below exist so a deployment
# that injects configuration rather than typing it still can.

# ── Set by install.sh ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the key that encrypts refresh tokens and API keys at rest.
# A file, never a value: an env var holding the key itself is readable from
# /proc/<pid>/environ and appears in container inspection output.
TOKEN_KEY_PATH=/home/you/.dashboard/token.key

# Where the database, log and certificate live. Created with mode 700.
DASHBOARD_DATA=/home/you/.dashboard

# ── Worth setting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The origin the dashboard is reached on, used to build the OAuth redirect
# URI. Must match what is registered in Google Cloud exactly, scheme and port
# included — a mismatch surfaces only as Google's redirect_uri_mismatch.
# Derived from the request when unset, which is right on a simple LAN setup
# and wrong behind a reverse proxy.
# BASE_URL=https://192.0.2.10:8766

# Comma-separated Google account `sub` values allowed to sign in. Empty means
# none, which is the safe default. Your sub is written to the log on the first
# rejected attempt.
# ALLOWED_GOOGLE_SUBS=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alternatives to entering these in Settings. The *_PATH forms are preferred:
# a path is not a credential, so it is safe in a unit file or an image.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_PATH=/run/secrets/google_client_secret
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/anthropic_api_key

# Shared with an external scheduler (n8n or similar) so it can trigger a sync.
# Unset means the ingest routes reject everything, which is the default.
# It opens no route that can read your data.
# INGEST_KEY=

# The one feature that can call a model: naming a category for a merchant
# nothing else recognised. It sends merchant names, your category names, and
# worked examples from your own filings — never amounts, dates, balances or
# account details. Off unless switched on in Settings, and it returns a
# label, never a number.
# CLASSIFY_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# ENABLE_LLM_CATEGORIES=true

# Log every HTTP request. Noisy; for debugging only.
# DASHBOARD_VERBOSE=1
